"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan with an initial budget of $500,000, kicking off on June 15th. The project has progressed through several phases: strategic partnerships with TechInnovate were established (and later explored again), and the team expanded to include five new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing (including Mike Chen and Lisa Ray). Key milestones include the completion of the design phase, the testing phase (celebrated on October 10th), and the transition to the development phase led by Omar Jensen. The project is currently focused on leveraging AI for data visualization, with a call for R&D proposals due by July 20th and a request for stakeholder feedback on the prototype due by the end of November."
